    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess. but even that \"just existing\" part feels so heavy. i mean, i'm writing him, but i'm also feeling it. like, when i'm sitting at my desk at 3am, it's not just the story. it's just this crushing sense that everything is pointless. if i'm being honest, the idea of him just \"breathing\" feels so unearned and... i don't know, annoying? it's like forcing a happy ending on something that doesn't deserve one. it would be more honest if he just stopped fighting it. if he just let the weight take him. does that make sense from a storytelling perspective? like, is a tragic end actually more \"real\" than a forced survival?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
